    "body": "`test_orphanage_dos_many` checks that a normal peer's orphan survives while DoS peers flood the orphanage. I found that the orphanage never fills: the 60 peers send the same 51 orphans as `tx`, and a `tx` already held as an orphan is dropped in `ReceivedTx` without recording its sender. The orphanage peaks at 152 announcements against a limit of 3000, so nothing is evicted.\n\nHere the first peer sends the orphans and the other 59 announce them by `inv`, which does add them as announcers. The test now asserts that the orphanage holds 3000 announcements, instead of asserting on what it sends. It takes about as long as before.\n\nIf `LimitOrphans` is changed to evict the normal peer's orphan first, the test used to pass and now fails. (`test_orphanage_dos_large` already catches that change.)\n\nFound while porting these tests to https://github.com/btclib-org/bitcoin-node-tests.\n\n*Made with my usual tools: a computer, the Internet and an LLM. The mistakes, as usual, are all mine.*\n\n",
